id: burning-hatred
name: Burning Hatred
order: 5
description: >
  You single out a foe, and when they can no longer provide any entertainment, you turn your vicious gaze to another.
text: >
  Burning Hatred: You single out a foe, and when they can no longer provide any entertainment, you turn your vicious gaze to another.
  (1)-[Triggered/Start of Combat Round, Ruling]: Select an Opponent, they become your ‘Enemy’. You gain the Compelled Combat Condition against your Enemy until the end of the Combat Round.
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase your Wound Rolls against your Enemy by 3(T).
  (3)-[Triggered]: If you Defeat your Enemy or knock them through a Health Threshold with your Attacking Maneuver, maximize your stacks of Overwhelm.

---

# (1) As each Combat Round starts: which Opponent on the scene - of another disposition than your token's - asked of
# whoever plays you, or none; your Enemy until another is chosen. Compelled till the Round ends - against them, the
# table's: who you were told to attack is not tracked (chat.mjs askEnemy). Automatic by default, asked every Round;
# set Triggered, ticked on the Round's card.
[triggered/start-of-round, effect 1]
chooseEnemy();

# (2) Against your Enemy, where the Wound is worked out per target (chat.mjs enemyParts).

# (3) Your Enemy Defeated, or knocked through a Health Threshold, by your Attacking Maneuver: Overwhelm at its most
# (Overwhelming Fighter's, 4). One Triggered/Automatic button for both.
[triggered/knock-through, effect 3]
requires fallenEnemy;
overwhelm.stacks = 4;

[triggered/defeat-opponent, effect 3]
requires fallenEnemy;
overwhelm.stacks = 4;
